    "chunk_text": "30. Any complaint about places where food is distributed or served free of charge for licensed promotional purposes may be made in writing or orally to the Chairman, Secretary or Authorized Officers and it shall be lawful for such officers to conduct a formal investigation.\n\n32. A person authorized by the Chairman, the Medical Officer of Health or the Public Health Inspector or the Chairman to act on or under any circumstance may seek to act without a permit under Section 3 above. It is lawful for a notice to be terminated by a written notice.\n\n57A IV(\u0d85) \u0dd9\u0d9a\u02a3\u0da7\u0dc3 - \u027c \u0dbd\u0d82\u0d9a\u0dcf \u021d\u0da2\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf\u01e6\u01b5\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0db8\u0dcf\u0da2\u0dc0\u0dcf\u01cf \u0da2\u0db1\u0dbb\u0da2\u0dd9\u024f \u0d85\u01af \u026a\u0dd9\u0dc1\u0dc2 \u0d9c\u0dd0\u0dc3\u0178 \u0db4\u01b4\u0dba - 2019.12.05 PART IV(A) \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 05.12.2019\n\n33. 122 (2) of the Pradeshiya Sabha Act No. 15 of 1987, which relates to the offense of maintaining a premises without a license required under this by-law or violating any of the provisions of the by-law. Shall be subject to a fine referred to in Sub-section. When a person who has been convicted of a wrongful offense by a court of competent jurisdiction over the offense continues to commit such violations or violations, a written notice may be submitted by the Chairman, the Medical Officer of Health or the Public Health Inspector. Every US who continues the violation after being given An additional fine of the above section shall also be liable to be imposed for a period of time.\n\n34. Unless the changers of the by-laws are necessary\n\n\"Chairman\" shall mean the person holding the office of the Chairman of the Pradeshiya Sabha for the duration of the term or performing the functions of that office,\n\n\u201cPradeshiya Sabha\u201d shall mean Rambukkana Pradeshiya Sabha,\n\n\"Medical Officer of Health\" shall mean the person holding the office of any Medical Officer of Health in the area of the Divisional Council area,\n\n\"Public Health Inspector\" shall mean any Public Health Inspector Division within the area of authority of the Divisional Secretariat,"
