    "chunk_size_bytes": 1699,
    "chunk_text": "II. All fruits and vegetables that can be eaten at the time of delivery should be washed before serving.\n\nIII. Stuffed vegetables should be kept in well ventilated, adequate lighting, no room for rats, or in any\n\nother room or refrigerator or cooler room.\n\n17. A place where food is intended to be distributed free of charge or served for any promotional purpose should not be a food hazard.\n\n18. The place shall be authorized by the Chairman so as not to cause any public obstruction or to cause any public disturbance\n\n19. It should be a temporary or permanent building designed to provide adequate space so that all operations can be carried out satisfactorily.\n\n20. The adjacent jar should be kept in place and garbage containers should be kept in such a way that flies or other insects cannot enter.\n\n21. In the event that the Pradeshiya Sabha intends to operate a free food place in an area not covered by the Solid Waste Management Service, a license must not be issued unless the applicant has established a formal waste disposal system as specified by the Medical Officer, Public Health Inspector.\n\n57A IV(\u0d85) \u0dd9\u0d9a\u02a3\u0da7\u0dc3 - \u027c \u0dbd\u0d82\u0d9a\u0dcf \u021d\u0da2\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf\u01e6\u01b5\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0db8\u0dcf\u0da2\u0dc0\u0dcf\u01cf \u0da2\u0db1\u0dbb\u0da2\u0dd9\u024f \u0d85\u01af \u026a\u0dd9\u0dc1\u0dc2 \u0d9c\u0dd0\u0dc3\u0178 \u0db4\u01b4\u0dba - 2019.12.05 PART IV(A) \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 05.12.2019\n\n22. It is the duty of the Licensee to ensure that employees wear the same hats at all times when they are employed, in order to ensure that every employee engaged in the preparation of meals at the Licensed Place.\n\n23. Provide clean water, clean towels and hand washing soap or lotion to everyone working in the licensed premises."
  },
