    "chunk_text": "(iii) Thrice the number of vacancies from among those who obtained the minimum marksand above required to pass the written examination will be called for the general interview.The general interview will be conducted by a Board of Interview appointed by the PublicService Commission.\n\n(v) A number of candidates equivalent to the number of vacancies will be recruited in theorder of merit of the aggregate of marks obtained at the written examination, interviewfor evaluating eligibility and practical test by the candidates who have secured minimummarks required to get a pass at the written examination and the practical test comingunder the interview for Evaluating Eligibility.\n\nWill be amended as\n\n(a) Marks will not be awarded.\n\nEvery term referred to as \u201cStructured Interview\u201d should be amended as \u201cInterview forEvaluating Eligibility.\u201d\n\nInterview for Evaluating Eligibility and Practical Test:\n\n(I) Interview for Evaluating Eligibility\n\n(a) Marks will be awarded for the ancillary qualifications obtained in addition to the basicqualifications in the following areas.\n\nMain headings for which marksTotalMinimumare awardedMarksMarks\n\n1. Additional educational qualifications20\n\n2. English language proficiency15\n\n3. Information Communication Technologyskill15\n\nTotal50\n\n7.2.2.1 (iv)\n\nSection No.Proposed Amendment\n\n7.2.4.\n\n(a) of 7.2.4.3\n\n7.2.4.4\n\nNotapplicable\n\nI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'12'09PART I : SEC. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 09.12.20193A\n\nNote:- (i) The Public Service Commission will approve a detailed marking scheme forthe interview for evaluating eligibility within the maximum marks allocated for themain areas for which marks are awarded as stated in part I of the table above.\n\n(II) Practical Test\n\n(a) This is a practical test for a presentation on a given topic relating to the subject.\n\nMain headings for which marksTotalMinimumare awardedMarksMarks\n\n1. Approach05"
